          "id": "ch14_ex16_q1a",
          "number": "1(a)",
          "category": null,
          "questionText": "Convert the following to radian measure in terms of $\\pi$: $330^\\circ$",
          "questionFigures": [],
          "solution": {
            "formula": "$1^\\circ = \\dfrac{\\pi}{180}$ radians, so $x^\\circ = \\dfrac{x\\pi}{180}$ radians",
            "steps": [
              "Given: $330^\\circ$. Goal: write it in radians as a multiple of $\\pi$.",
              "Multiply by $\\dfrac{\\pi}{180}$: $330^\\circ = \\dfrac{330\\pi}{180}$",
              "Simplify by dividing top and bottom by 30: $\\dfrac{330}{180} = \\dfrac{11}{6}$",
              "So $330^\\circ = \\dfrac{11\\pi}{6}$.",
              "Check: $\\dfrac{11\\pi}{6} \\times \\dfrac{180}{\\pi} = 11 \\times 30 = 330$ ✓"
            ],
            "finalAnswer": "$\\dfrac{11\\pi}{6}$",
            "solutionFigures": [],
            "tip": "Degrees to radians: multiply by $\\pi/180$; radians to degrees: multiply by $180/\\pi$."
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "ch14_ex16_q1b",
          "number": "1(b)",
          "category": null,
          "questionText": "Convert the following to radian measure in terms of $\\pi$: $810^\\circ$",
          "questionFigures": [],
          "solution": {
            "formula": "$x^\\circ = \\dfrac{x\\pi}{180}$ radians",
            "steps": [
              "Given: $810^\\circ$. Goal: radians in terms of $\\pi$.",
              "$810^\\circ = \\dfrac{810\\pi}{180}$",
              "Divide top and bottom by 90: $\\dfrac{810}{180} = \\dfrac{9}{2}$",
              "So $810^\\circ = \\dfrac{9\\pi}{2}$.",
              "Check: $\\dfrac{9}{2} \\times 180 = 810$ ✓"
            ],
            "finalAnswer": "$\\dfrac{9\\pi}{2}$",
            "solutionFigures": [],
            "tip": "Angles larger than $360^\\circ$ convert in exactly the same way; there is no need to subtract $360^\\circ$ first."
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "ch14_ex16_q1c",
          "number": "1(c)",
          "category": null,
          "questionText": "Convert the following to radian measure in terms of $\\pi$: $1080^\\circ$",
          "questionFigures": [],
          "solution": {
            "formula": "$x^\\circ = \\dfrac{x\\pi}{180}$ radians",
            "steps": [
              "Given: $1080^\\circ$. Goal: radians in terms of $\\pi$.",
              "$1080^\\circ = \\dfrac{1080\\pi}{180}$",
              "$\\dfrac{1080}{180} = 6$",
              "So $1080^\\circ = 6\\pi$ (three full turns, since $360^\\circ = 2\\pi$).",
              "Check: $6 \\times 180 = 1080$ ✓"
            ],
            "finalAnswer": "$6\\pi$",
            "solutionFigures": [],
            "tip": "Each full turn of $360^\\circ$ is $2\\pi$, so $1080^\\circ = 3 \\times 2\\pi$."
          }
        },
