          "questionText": "Convert the following to degree measure: $\\dfrac{5\\pi^c}{6}$",
          "questionFigures": [],
          "solution": {
            "formula": "$1^c = \\dfrac{180^\\circ}{\\pi}$, so $\\theta^c = \\theta \\times \\dfrac{180}{\\pi}$ degrees",
            "steps": [
              "Given: $\\frac{5\\pi}{6}$ radians. Goal: degrees.",
              "Multiply by $\\dfrac{180}{\\pi}$: $\\dfrac{5\\pi}{6} \\times \\dfrac{180}{\\pi} = 5 \\times 30$",
              "$= 150^\\circ$",
              "So $\\dfrac{5\\pi^c}{6} = 150^\\circ$."
            ],
            "finalAnswer": "$150^\\circ$",
            "solutionFigures": [],
            "tip": "Shortcut: replace $\\pi$ by $180^\\circ$, then simplify: $\\frac{5 \\times 180}{6} = 150$."
          }
