        {
          "id": "ch14_ex16_q3a",
          "number": "3(a)",
          "category": null,
          "questionText": "Give the exact value of $\\sin\\left(\\dfrac{11\\pi}{4}\\right)$",
          "questionFigures": [],
          "solution": {
            "formula": "Periodicity $\\sin(\\theta + 2k\\pi) = \\sin\\theta$; symmetry $\\sin(\\pi - \\theta) = \\sin\\theta$; $\\sin\\frac{\\pi}{4} = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}$",
            "steps": [
              "Given: $\\sin\\frac{11\\pi}{4}$. Goal: exact value.",
              "Remove a full turn: $\\dfrac{11\\pi}{4} - 2\\pi = \\dfrac{11\\pi}{4} - \\dfrac{8\\pi}{4} = \\dfrac{3\\pi}{4}$, so $\\sin\\frac{11\\pi}{4} = \\sin\\frac{3\\pi}{4}$",
              "$\\frac{3\\pi}{4} = \\pi - \\frac{\\pi}{4}$ is in quadrant 2, where sine is positive.",
              "$\\sin\\left(\\pi - \\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right) = \\sin\\frac{\\pi}{4} = \\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} = \\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$",
              "So $\\sin\\frac{11\\pi}{4} = \\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$."
            ],
            "finalAnswer": "$\\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$ (that is, $\\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}$)",
            "solutionFigures": [],
            "tip": "Reduce by multiples of $2\\pi$ first, then use the quadrant to decide the sign."
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "ch14_ex16_q3b",
          "number": "3(b)",
          "category": null,
          "questionText": "Give the exact value of $\\cos\\left(-\\dfrac{7\\pi}{4}\\right)$",
          "questionFigures": [],
          "solution": {
            "formula": "$\\cos(-\\theta) = \\cos\\theta$; $\\cos(2\\pi - \\theta) = \\cos\\theta$; $\\cos\\frac{\\pi}{4} = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}$",
            "steps": [
              "Given: $\\cos\\left(-\\frac{7\\pi}{4}\\right)$. Goal: exact value.",
              "Cosine is even: $\\cos\\left(-\\frac{7\\pi}{4}\\right) = \\cos\\frac{7\\pi}{4}$",
              "$\\frac{7\\pi}{4} = 2\\pi - \\frac{\\pi}{4}$ is in quadrant 4, where cosine is positive.",
              "$\\cos\\left(2\\pi - \\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right) = \\cos\\frac{\\pi}{4} = \\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$",
              "Check: $-\\frac{7\\pi}{4} + 2\\pi = \\frac{\\pi}{4}$, and $\\cos\\frac{\\pi}{4} = \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$ ✓"
            ],
            "finalAnswer": "$\\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$",
            "solutionFigures": [],
            "tip": "$\\cos(-\\theta) = \\cos\\theta$ but $\\sin(-\\theta) = -\\sin\\theta$: do not mix them up."
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "ch14_ex16_q3c",
          "number": "3(c)",
          "category": null,
          "questionText": "Give the exact value of $\\sin\\left(\\dfrac{11\\pi}{6}\\right)$",
          "questionFigures": [],
          "solution": {
            "formula": "$\\sin(2\\pi - \\theta) = -\\sin\\theta$; $\\sin\\frac{\\pi}{6} = \\frac{1}{2}$",
            "steps": [
              "Given: $\\sin\\frac{11\\pi}{6}$. Goal: exact value.",
              "$\\frac{11\\pi}{6} = 2\\pi - \\frac{\\pi}{6}$, which is in quadrant 4, where sine is negative.",
              "$\\sin\\left(2\\pi - \\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right) = -\\sin\\frac{\\pi}{6} = -\\dfrac{1}{2}$",
              "So $\\sin\\frac{11\\pi}{6} = -\\frac{1}{2}$."
            ],
            "finalAnswer": "$-\\dfrac{1}{2}$",
            "solutionFigures": [],
            "tip": "In quadrant 4 only cosine is positive."
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "ch14_ex16_q3d",
          "number": "3(d)",
          "category": null,
          "questionText": "Give the exact value of $\\cos\\left(-\\dfrac{7\\pi}{6}\\right)$",
          "questionFigures": [],
          "solution": {
            "formula": "$\\cos(-\\theta) = \\cos\\theta$; $\\cos(\\pi + \\theta) = -\\cos\\theta$; $\\cos\\frac{\\pi}{6} = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$",
            "steps": [
              "Given: $\\cos\\left(-\\frac{7\\pi}{6}\\right)$. Goal: exact value.",
              "Cosine is even: $\\cos\\left(-\\frac{7\\pi}{6}\\right) = \\cos\\frac{7\\pi}{6}$",
              "$\\frac{7\\pi}{6} = \\pi + \\frac{\\pi}{6}$ is in quadrant 3, where cosine is negative.",
              "$\\cos\\left(\\pi + \\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right) = -\\cos\\frac{\\pi}{6} = -\\dfrac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$",
              "So $\\cos\\left(-\\frac{7\\pi}{6}\\right) = -\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$."
            ],
            "finalAnswer": "$-\\dfrac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$",
            "solutionFigures": [],
            "tip": "Find the quadrant before writing the value; the sign comes from the quadrant."
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "ch14_ex16_q3e",
          "number": "3(e)",
          "category": null,
          "questionText": "Give the exact value of $\\cos\\left(\\dfrac{13\\pi}{6}\\right)$",
          "questionFigures": [],
          "solution": {
            "formula": "$\\cos(\\theta + 2\\pi) = \\cos\\theta$; $\\cos\\frac{\\pi}{6} = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$",
            "steps": [
              "Given: $\\cos\\frac{13\\pi}{6}$. Goal: exact value.",
              "$\\frac{13\\pi}{6} = 2\\pi + \\frac{\\pi}{6}$, one full turn plus $\\frac{\\pi}{6}$ (quadrant 1).",
              "$\\cos\\frac{13\\pi}{6} = \\cos\\frac{\\pi}{6} = \\dfrac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$"
            ],
            "finalAnswer": "$\\dfrac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$",
            "solutionFigures": [],
            "tip": "Subtracting $2\\pi = \\frac{12\\pi}{6}$ leaves the same point on the unit circle."
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "ch14_ex16_q3f",
          "number": "3(f)",
          "category": null,
          "questionText": "Give the exact value of $\\sin\\left(\\dfrac{23\\pi}{6}\\right)$",
          "questionFigures": [],
          "solution": {
            "formula": "$\\sin(\\theta + 2k\\pi) = \\sin\\theta$; $\\sin(-\\theta) = -\\sin\\theta$; $\\sin\\frac{\\pi}{6} = \\frac{1}{2}$",
            "steps": [
              "Given: $\\sin\\frac{23\\pi}{6}$. Goal: exact value.",
              "$\\frac{23\\pi}{6} = 4\\pi - \\frac{\\pi}{6}$ (since $4\\pi = \\frac{24\\pi}{6}$).",
              "Remove two full turns: $\\sin\\frac{23\\pi}{6} = \\sin\\left(-\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right)$",
              "Sine is odd: $\\sin\\left(-\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right) = -\\sin\\frac{\\pi}{6} = -\\dfrac{1}{2}$",
              "So $\\sin\\frac{23\\pi}{6} = -\\frac{1}{2}$ (the point is in quadrant 4)."
            ],
            "finalAnswer": "$-\\dfrac{1}{2}$",
            "solutionFigures": [],
            "tip": "Writing the angle as (multiple of $2\\pi$) $\\pm$ (basic angle) is often the quickest route."
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "ch14_ex16_q3g",
